// CompactCart defines model for CompactCart.
type CompactCart struct {
	// Available Choices per checkout field. Every field has `required` and `type`. Fields with a choice list it under `options`: shipping and payment methods with `id`, `name` and `description`, shipping options with `id`, `name` and `description` (hint for the option, `null` if none is set), partial delivery with `id` and `name` (`partialDelivery` lists `partial` and is `required` only while a product of the cart is out of stock; otherwise only `complete` is listed and `required` is `false`), shipping addresses with `id`, `default`, the address fields and `type` (`billing` for the billing address, `shipping` for every other address, like in `GET /store-api/v1/account/customer`). The billing address can be selected as shipping address, but it cannot be changed or deleted. `shippingAddressId.options` only contains the addresses the selected shipping method delivers to, e.g. for local delivery only the addresses within its delivery area; the other addresses can be selected with another shipping method. `termsAccepted` has the type `boolean`: send `termsAccepted: true` with `POST /store-api/v1/checkout/order`. `shippingMethodId.options` and `paymentMethodId.options` only contain the methods available for the current cart and customer; payment methods also depend on the selected shipping method. Both lists start with the default method of the shop, followed by the other methods in a fixed order. They are recalculated with every cart response and may be empty. Only fields that apply to the selected shipping method are listed: for pickup there is no `shippingAddressId`, and `selected.shippingAddress` is `null`. `shippingOptionId` is only listed, and then required, when the shipping method has at least two options; a single option applies without a choice and is reported in `selected.shippingOptionId`. `shippingAddOns` (type `booleanMap`, never required) lists the optional services of the selected shipping option (e.g. forklift, phone notice) in display order, with `id`, `name`, `description` (`null` if none is set), `price` (net amount in EUR, `null` if there is no price) and `defaultValue`; it is left out when the option offers none. Set a value with `POST /store-api/v1/checkout/set-shipping-add-on`. Show only the fields contained in `available`.
	Available map[string]interface{} `json:"available"`
	Items     []struct {
		// ListPrice Net list price of the position (price for all customers at quantity 1), to show struck through next to `price`. Set only when `price.unit` is below `listPrice.unit`. `null` for sets and bundles, for articles without a price for all customers, for guests and customers who cannot see prices, when the cart shows gross prices and when the customer's price is not lower.
		ListPrice *struct {
			// Total `unit` × `quantity`, rounded to two decimals.
			Total float32 `json:"total"`

			// Unit List price of one unit.
			Unit float32 `json:"unit"`
		} `json:"listPrice"`
	} `json:"items"`

	// Notices Messages about the last cart change. A message without `productId` is shown once per context; notices with `productId` come with every rejection or change, also repeated ones. Show `message` to the customer and decide by `code`, never by the wording of `message`.
	//
	// | `code` | Meaning |
	// |---|---|
	// | `CHECKOUT__LINE_ITEM_BLOCKED` | A product of the request cannot be ordered: it has no price for the customer, its price is on request, or it is a packaging unit that is not listed in `variants` of its product. Nothing of the request was added; do not show the products as added. `productId` is that product; for a set it is the component that cannot be ordered, not the set. |
	// | `CHECKOUT__LINE_ITEM_REMOVED` | A position was removed from the cart because its product has no price (any more), is a packaging unit that is no longer listed in `variants` of its product, or became unavailable. `productId` is the product of that position. |
	// | `CHECKOUT__UNIT_VARIANTS_COMBINED` | Level `0`, the cart stays orderable. The quantity of an article was moved onto its packaging units, largest first (e.g. 25 pieces became 1 box), after `POST /store-api/v1/checkout/cart/line-item` or a quantity change. One notice per position that was created or got another quantity; `productId` is the product of that position. Only in the response of that request. |
	// | `CHECKOUT__CUSTOMER_PURCHASE_NOT_ALLOWED` | The customer is not unlocked for orders (`customerState: LOCKED` in `GET /store-api/v1/account/customer`), but the cart still has products from before the lock. The positions stay; `POST /store-api/v1/checkout/order` is rejected with the same code. |
	// | `CHECKOUT__GERMAN_VAT_ID_REQUIRED` | The billing address is outside Germany, the delivery goes to Germany and the customer has no German VAT ID (AG-732). `POST /store-api/v1/checkout/order` is rejected with the same code; let the customer choose a delivery address in the billing country. |
	// | `CHECKOUT__DELIVERY_COUNTRY_VAT_ID_REQUIRED` | The delivery goes to an EU country other than Germany and the customer has no VAT ID of that country (AG-732). `POST /store-api/v1/checkout/order` is rejected with the same code; let the customer choose a delivery address in Germany. |
	// | `CHECKOUT__SHIPPING_METHOD_NOT_AVAILABLE`, `CHECKOUT__PAYMENT_METHOD_NOT_AVAILABLE` | The selected shipping or payment method is not available for the current cart; same codes as `POST /store-api/v1/checkout/order`. |
	//
	// All other notices get `CHECKOUT__` plus the error key of the shop, e.g. `CHECKOUT__PRODUCT_OUT_OF_STOCK`, the same code `POST /store-api/v1/checkout/order` reports when the notice blocks the order. Show `message` for codes you do not know.
	//
	// A missing login never comes as a notice: `POST /store-api/v1/checkout/cart/line-item` answers `401` with the error `CHECKOUT__CUSTOMER_LOGIN_REQUIRED`, and the cart of a guest has no notice for it.
	Notices []struct {
		// Code Stable, machine-readable code of the notice (see the table above).
		Code string `json:"code"`

		// Level Severity: `0` notice, `10` warning, `20` error.
		Level CompactCartNoticesLevel `json:"level"`

		// Message German sentence for the customer.
		Message string `json:"message"`

		// ProductId Product the notice is about, `null` when it concerns no single product.
		ProductId *string `json:"productId"`
	} `json:"notices"`

	// Selected Current checkout values. `shippingAddress` has the same fields as the addresses in `available.shippingAddressId.options`, including `type`. `shippingMethodId` and `paymentMethodId` are `null` when the method stored in the context is not (or no longer) contained in the corresponding `available` list, e.g. because the cart changed; the client must then let the customer choose again. `shippingAddress` is `null` when the stored address is not contained in `available.shippingAddressId.options` because the selected shipping method does not deliver there. The shipping method then stays selected as long as it delivers to at least one other address of the customer; the client must let the customer choose one of the listed addresses. Until then `POST /store-api/v1/checkout/order` rejects the order with `CHECKOUT__SHIPPING_METHOD_NOT_AVAILABLE`. `shippingDate` is `null` when the stored date is no longer possible: the earliest date (`available.shippingDate.earliest`) moves with the time of day, so a date chosen in the morning can be too early in the afternoon. `POST /store-api/v1/checkout/order` rejects such a date with `422` `CHECKOUT__INVALID_DELIVERY_DATE`; let the customer choose a new date. `shippingOptionId` is the option that applies: the chosen one, or the only option of the shipping method, which applies without a choice and is not listed in `available`. `partialDelivery` is `complete` as soon as the cart no longer offers partial delivery (the product is in stock again or was removed): a chosen `partial` then expires, also for the order, and has to be chosen again if a product runs out of stock later. `shippingAddOns` maps the ID of every add-on the selected shipping option offers to its value (`true` booked, `false` not booked); values the customer has not set yet are the add-on defaults. It is `null` when no shipping option applies or the option offers no add-ons.
	Selected map[string]interface{} `json:"selected"`
	Totals   struct {
		// Gross Total including VAT; equals `net` for a tax-free cart.
		Gross *float32 `json:"gross"`

		// Net Net total of the cart.
		Net *float32 `json:"net"`

		// Savings Net amount the customer saves against the list prices: sum of `listPrice.total` − `price.total` over all positions with `listPrice`, rounded to two decimals. `null` when no position has a list price.
		Savings *float32 `json:"savings"`

		// TaxExemption Why the cart is tax-free, `null` when it is not (AG-732). Show `message` next to the totals as long as the field is set; decide by `code`.
		//
		// | `code` | Meaning |
		// |---|---|
		// | `INTRA_COMMUNITY_DELIVERY` | The delivery goes to an EU country other than Germany and the customer has a VAT ID of that country (e.g. `ATU…` for Austria), whatever the billing country: no German VAT. |
		TaxExemption *struct {
			Code    CompactCartTotalsTaxExemptionCode `json:"code"`
			Message string                            `json:"message"`
		} `json:"taxExemption"`

		// Vat VAT per rate. Empty for a tax-free cart: then show no VAT line at all, also not 0 %.
		Vat []struct {
			Amount *float32 `json:"amount,omitempty"`
			Rate   *float32 `json:"rate,omitempty"`
		} `json:"vat"`
	} `json:"totals"`
}

